Shared typography, logical-DIP design tokens and icon presentation/cache helpers retain the existing app-owned asset provenance. Raster resizing uses the already-pinned image 0.25.8 crate (MIT OR Apache-2.0); this library enables no image codecs. Artwork and font files remain app-owned and are not redistributed by sk-iced.
Stage-two cached viewports, column header/resize gestures, selection and tree navigation adapt File Beholder code (MIT; copyright 2026 File Beholder contributors). New data-component builders retain Apache-2.0 provenance. Domain-specific models, workers and assets remain app-owned. No additional dependency is introduced.
Stage-three split geometry, tab viewport/surface, responsive toolbar measurement, drag markers/collection and drop painting retain File Beholder MIT provenance (copyright 2026 File Beholder contributors). New navigation/toolbar composition is Apache-2.0. App-owned routes, workspace/file transactions and diagnostic reorder snapshots remain local. No new dependency is introduced.
Stage-four form/feedback/viewer composition, labeled progress and the component catalog are Apache-2.0. ShareMeter, FillClip, ResizeGrip and the transparent interaction-gate foundation retain File Beholder MIT provenance (copyright 2026 File Beholder contributors). The selectable viewer retains the existing PC Tonic software-renderer presentation. App-owned content, validation, reports and actions remain local. No new dependency is introduced.
